    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup is anchored today by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.27), who both draw favorable matchups against pitchers with xERAs near 5.00. **Gunnar Henderson** is the clear priority, benefiting from a high-efficiency batting order spot and a strong +16% boost due to the matchup against Arrighetti. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) projects as a cornerstone of today's production; he is currently enjoying a high-ceiling environment where park factors and a friendly platoon split against J.T. Ginn provide a significant lift. **Jacob Wilson** (71.63) and **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) round out our most reliable options, with **Sam Antonacci** maintaining high value despite the difficult hurdle of Bieber, thanks largely to his leadoff role and the +10% order bonus.\n\nOur most difficult decision of the day involved the benching of **Nasim Nunez** (58.79), who finished just shy of the starting threshold. While **Nasim Nunez** offers the switch-hitting versatility and park-aided upside we covet, the optimizer penalized his projected spot in the #9 hole, which curtailed his run-production potential relative to the rest of the utility infielders. Conversely, we are keeping a cautious eye on **Kyle Tucker** (55.62) and **Andy Pages** (51.65). Both are facing a high-skill arm in Ryan Weathers, and their scores are suppressed by the -14% SP Skill penalty. We are also monitoring the lineup status of **Heliot Ramos** (44.20); he is hovering dangerously close to our \"Below Floor\" category due to a poor park factor and a matchup against Bryan Woo, making him a candidate for mid-game substitution if he does not show early effectiveness.",
